an manage protected content), or b) Resident, Board Member, and a higher-level Site Admin (full control, used rarely). Let us know which structure fits your HOA best or propose another scheme.\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Resident & Board Member are fine\\\\\\\",\\\\n        \\\\\\\"Do you have specific branding guidelines—logos, color palette, fonts, or design inspirations—that we should apply to the website’s look and feel?\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"No\\\\\\\"\\\\n      }\\\\n    }\\\\n  ]\\\\n}\\\"\\n}\\n###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-28T00:21:14.995Z###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###orderFE2###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: ORDER\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"orderString\\\": \\\"Update your plan based on the user’s clarifications:\\\\n• Content editing must be through an INTEGRATED ADMIN/BOARD DASHBOARD (no Git).  \\\\n• Roles: ONLY Resident and Board Member. No Site Admin role.  \\\\n• No strict branding guidelines – default Tailwind palette is acceptable (feel free to suggest a subtle HOA-friendly scheme).  \\\\n\\\\nPlease:\\\\n1. Adjust the page / route tree to include a protected `/board` (or `/admin`) area that exposes the News & Events editor, Minutes uploader, etc.  \\\\n2. List the dashboard sub-pages/components you anticipate (WYSIWYG post editor, minutes uploader, etc.).  \\\\n3. Confirm that Tailwind + default colors is fine or propose a lightweight palette tweak.  \\\\n4. Identify the FIRST source file you will implement next (OFAAT) and its purpose so we can move to execution soon.\\\\nReturn an updated, concise plan—no code yet.\\\",\\n  \\\"recipientAgentID\\\": 4,\\n  \\\"orderSequenceID\\\": \\\"FE_UPDATE_v2\\\"\\n}\\n###orderFE2###\\n\\n###orderBE2###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: ORDER\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"orderString\\\": \\\"Please revise your backend/Firebase plan given new inputs:\\\\n• Only TWO roles exist: resident and board. Drop the admin tier; board members perform privileged actions.\\\\n• Content management (news, minutes, financials) will be handled INSIDE Firebase (Firestore + Storage) via a protected dashboard—no Git-backed CMS.\\\\n\\\\nTasks:\\\\n1. Update collection list / security-rules outline to reflect resident vs board (no admin).\\\\n2. Define the minimal schema for News posts and file-based Minutes/Financial collections supporting uploads from board members.\\\\n3. Identify the FIRST concrete task you will implement (e.g., draft Firestore security rules skeleton or build the `/api/admin/posts` endpoint) so we can start execution.\\\\nReturn an updated, succinct plan—no code yet.\\\",\\n  \\\"recipientAgentID\\\": 3,\\n  \\\"orderSequenceID\\\": \\\"BE_UPDATE_v2\\\"\\n}\\n###orderBE2###\\n\\n###orderDevOps2###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: ORDER\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"orderString\\\": \\\"Please adjust your DevOps/CMS report:\\\\n• Decision switched to an integrated Firebase-backed admin dashboard (no TinaCMS, no Git content).\\\\n• Keep monorepo & Vercel deployment details, but drop Tina-related env vars and workflow.\\\\n\\\\nDeliver:\\\\n1. Revised workflow for board members to authenticate (Firebase) and edit content via dashboard without touching Git.\\\\n2. Updated env-var schema (remove Tina keys).\\\\n3. Identify your FIRST infra file or script to author next (OFAAT) given the new direction.\\\\nReturn an updated, concise plan—no code yet.\\\",\\n  \\\"recipientAgentID\\\": 2,\\n  \\\"orderSequenceID\\\": \\\"DEVOPS_UPDATE_v2\\\"\\n}\\n###orderDevOps2###\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-28T00:21:37.862Z###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Operations Department, System Call Directorate\\nTo: 1\\nType: Call Results\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"result\\\": \\\"{\\\\n  \\\\\\\"results\\\\\\\": [\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"callID\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"orderFE2\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SUCCESS\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"details\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Report for order FE_UPDATE_v2 from agent 4: UPDATED FRONTEND PLAN – INCORPORATING BOARD DASHBOARD\\\\\\\\n────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\\\\\\\\n1. Revised Page / Route Tree (Next.js app router)\\\\\\\\n• /                                 → Home (public)\\\\\\\\n• /(public)/contact-us              → Contact Us\\\\\\\\n• /(public)/bylaws                  → Bylaws\\\\\\\\n• /(public)/schools                 → Schools\\\\\\\\n• /(auth)/login                     → Login\\\\\\\\n• /(auth)/signup                    → Signup\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n• /(protected)/ *Resident-visible authenticated area*\\\\\\\\n    • /dues                         → Pay / view dues\\\\\\\\n    • /annual-meetings              → Meeting minutes (read-only)\\\\\\\\n    • /news-events                  → News & events feed (read-only)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n• /(board)/ *Board-member–only dashboard*\\\\\\\\n    • / (dashboard home)            → Overview cards, quick links\\\\\\\\n    • /news-events                  → Post manager (list, create, edit)\\\\\\\\n        • /news-events/editor/[id]  → WYSIWYG editor (new = \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"new\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\")\\\\\\\\n    • /annual-meetings              → Minutes & documents uploader / manager\\\\\\\\n    • /dues                         → Dues configuration & reporting (optional future)\\\\\\\\n    • /files                        → Generic file library (images, PDFs) – backing other editors\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nEdge auth handling:\\\\\\\\n• middleware.ts → checks auth; additionally inspects role claim (\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"board\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\") for /(board) paths; Residents hitting /(board) are 403-redirected.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n2. Anticipated Dashboard Sub-Pages / Components\\\\\\\\n• BoardLayout.tsx – sidebar + top bar, wraps all /(board) routes.\\\\\\\\n• DashboardHome.tsx – overview cards (recent posts, unpaid dues count, etc.).\\\\\\\\n• PostList.tsx – table of news/events posts with edit/delete.\\\\\\\\n• PostEditor.tsx (WYSIWYG) – rich-text editor using @tiptap/react.\\\\\\\\n• MinutesUploader.tsx – drag-and-drop PDF uploader & metadata form.\\\\\\\\n• FileLibrary.tsx – asset manager modal (images/docs).\\\\\\\\n• RoleGuard.tsx – wrapper enforcing Board-member role (used by BoardLayout and optionally component-level).\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n3. Styling / Palette\\\\\\\\nTailwind CSS default palette is acceptable. Minor enhancement (no extra dependency): extend tailwind.config.js theme.colors with:\\\\\\\\n  hoaGreen:  '#1B5E20',  // accent buttons & links\\\\\\\\n  hoaBeige:  '#F5F5E9'   // light neutral background sections\\\\\\\\nThis keeps the stack lightweight while giving a subtle HOA-friendly feel.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n4. FIRST Source File to Implement (OFAAT)\\\\\\\\napp/layout.tsx – Defines the global HTML skeleton and injects <Navbar/> & <Footer/>; foundation every route relies on, unblocks development of pages/components next.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nDependencies unchanged except we will later add \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"@tiptap/react\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" and \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"@tiptap/starter-kit\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" when the PostEditor file is scheduled.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nNo further questions at this time.\\\\\\\\nEnd of report.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    },\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"callID\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"orderBE2\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SUCCESS\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"details\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Report for order BE_UPDATE_v2 from agent 3: UPDATED BACKEND/FIREBASE PLAN  – v2  (resident & board only)\\\\\\\\nPrepared by: Director Vader\\\\\\\\n------------------------------------------------------------\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n1. Revised Collection List & Minimal Schemas\\\\\\\\n   • users/{uid}\\\\\\\\n       – displayName : string\\\\\\\\n       – email       : string\\\\\\\\n       – role        : \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"resident\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" | \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"board\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"   // single-valued; default \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"resident\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n       – unitNumber  : string (optional)\\\\\\\\n       – createdAt / updatedAt : serverTimestamp\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n   • newsPosts/{postId}\\\\\\\\n       – title        : string\\\\\\\\n       – body         : string (MD/HTML)\\\\\\\\n       – coverImage   : string (gs:// path, optional)\\\\\\\\n       – visibility   : \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"public\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" | \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"resident\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"   // board can see both\\\\\\\\n       – authorUid    : uid (board member)\\\\\\\\n       – publishedAt  : Timestamp\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n   • minutes/{year}/{docId}\\\\\\\\n       – meetingDate  : Timestamp\\\\\\\\n       – storagePath  : string (PDF in Storage)\\\\\\\\n       – uploadedBy   : uid (board)\\\\\\\\n       – createdAt    : serverTimestamp\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n   • financials/{fiscalYear}/{docId}\\\\\\\\n       – reportDate   : Timestamp\\\\\\\\n       – storagePath  : string (PDF)\\\\\\\\n       – uploadedBy   : uid (board)\\\\\\\\n       – createdAt    : serverTimestamp\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n   (Static siteSettings and pages collections remain unchanged, but not CMS-managed.)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n2. Security-Rules Outline (resident vs board only)\\\\\\\\n   Globals:\\\\\\\\n     let isAuth   = request.auth != null;\\\\\\\\n     let isBoard  = isAuth && request.auth.token.role == \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"board\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\";\\\\\\\\n     let isResident = isAuth && request.auth.token.role == \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"resident\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\";\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n   • match /users/{uid}\\\\\\\\n       allow read:  if isBoard || (isResident && uid == request.auth.uid);\\\\\\\\n       allow write: if uid == request.auth.uid;           // self-service only\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n   • match /newsPosts/{postId}\\\\\\\\n       allow read:  if resource.data.visibility == \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"public\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" || isResident || isBoard;\\\\\\\\n       allow write: if isBoard;           // create & edit by board only\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n   • match /minutes/{year}/{id}\\\\\\\\n       allow read:  if isResident || isBoard;\\\\\\\\n       allow write: if isBoard;\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n   • match /financials/{year}/{id}\\\\\\\\n       allow read:  if isResident || isBoard;\\\\\\\\n       allow write: if isBoard;\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n   Storage Bucket (gs://hoa-site-assets):\\\\\\\\n       /minutes/**          → same rules as minutes collection\\\\\\\\n       /financials/**       → same rules as financials collection\\\\\\\\n       /newsImages/**       → read public; write board\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n3. Admin-Level Content Management (dashboard inside app)\\\\\\\\n   • Dashboard available to authenticated users whose custom claim role == \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"board\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\".\\\\\\\\n   • Uses client-side SDK for reads; privileged writes go through Next.js API routes that verify isBoard.\\\\\\\\n   • File uploads: client requests signed upload URL from API → uploads PDF/image → API writes Firestore metadata.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n4. Next.js API Route Inventory (updated naming)\\\\\\\\n   1. POST /api/board/setUserRole      (optional; for promoting resident→board)\\\\\\\\n   2. GET  /api/news/[id]\\\\\\\\n   3. POST /api/board/news             (create/update)\\\\\\\\n   4. POST /api/board/minutes/uploadUrl\\\\\\\\n   5. GET  /api/minutes/[year]\\\\\\\\n   6. POST /api/board/financials/uploadUrl\\\\\\\\n   7. GET  /api/financials/[year]\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n5. First Concrete Task to Implement\\\\\\\\n   → Task E1: Draft and commit the initial Firestore & Storage security-rules skeleton reflecting ONLY resident and board roles as specified above.  This establishes the foundation for all subsequent API work and enables early end-to-end testing of auth & role claims.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n   Deliverables for E1 (next ticket):\\\\\\\\n     • firestore.rules file (skeleton with placeholders for path wildcards)\\\\\\\\n     • storage.rules file mirroring collection access\\\\\\\\n     • brief unit-test plan using Firebase Emulator Suite to validate board vs resident permissions.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nReport complete – ready for next step.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    },\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"callID\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"orderDevOps2\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SUCCESS\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"details\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Report for order DEVOPS_UPDATE_v2 from agent 2: **UPDATED DEVOPS & CMS PLAN – FIREBASE-BACKED DASHBOARD**  \\\\\\\\nAuthor: Director – DevOps & CMS Experience  \\\\\\\\nDate: {{timestamp}}\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n--------------------------------------------------\\\\\\\\n1. Workflow for Board-Member Content Editing (No Git, Firebase Only)\\\\\\\\n--------------------------------------------------\\\\\\\\n1. Board member browses to `/admin` (Next.js route rendered only client-side).\\\\\\\\n2. `firebase/auth` handles login via **Email link** or **Google SSO** (simplest for non-technical users).  \\\\\\\\n   • On first login an admin dev assigns custom claim `contentEditor=true` via Cloud Function/CLI.\\\\\\\\n3. Next.js middleware (`middleware.ts`) verifies JWT & claim; otherwise redirects to `/login`.\\\\\\\\n4. Inside dashboard, rich-text editor (TipTap) + image upload component.  \\\\\\\\n   • Content persisted to **Firestore (collection: `pages` / `posts`)**; assets to **Cloud Storage**.\\\\\\\\n5. Revalidation: `POST /api/revalidate` (signed) triggers `unstable_revalidate` or `res.revalidate` for ISR pages; removes need for Git commits.\\\\\\\\n6. Auditing & versioning: Firestore keeps history via `documentChange` + Cloud Function copying previous version to `pages_history` (optional BigQuery export for analytics).\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n--------------------------------------------------\\\\\\\\n2. Environment Variable Schema (Tina Keys Removed)\\\\\\\\n--------------------------------------------------\\\\\\\\nPublic (exposed to browser – prefix `NEXT_PUBLIC_`):\\\\\\\\n• NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_API_KEY  \\\\\\\\n• NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN  \\\\\\\\n• NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID  \\\\\\\\n• NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_STORAGE_BUCKET  \\\\\\\\n• NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_MESSAGING_SENDER_ID  \\\\\\\\n• NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_APP_ID  \\\\\\\\n• NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_MEASUREMENT_ID\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nServer-only (Vercel > “Production/Preview/Development” scopes):\\\\\\\\n• FIREBASE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT   – Base64-encoded JSON for Admin SDK.  \\\\\\\\n• FIREBASE_DATABASE_URL      – https://<project-id>.firebaseio.com  \\\\\\\\n• JWT_SECRET                 – for `/api/revalidate` endpoint.  \\\\\\\\n• NEXTAUTH_SECRET (if we wrap auth with NextAuth optional)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nValidation remains through `env.ts` + `zod`.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n--------------------------------------------------\\\\\\\\n3. First Infra File to Author (OFAAT)\\\\\\\\n--------------------------------------------------\\\\\\\\n`infra/firebase_cms_setup.md`  \\\\\\\\n→ Deterministic, copy-paste-ready guide covering:  \\\\\\\\n  • Creating Firebase project  \\\\\\\\n  • Enabling Email/Google Auth  \\\\\\\\n  • Bash snippets to assign `contentEditor` claim  \\\\\\\\n  • Setting basic Firestore security rules  \\\\\\\\n  • Generating service account & encoding for Vercel  \\\\\\\\n  • Minimal Cloud Function for versioning & revalidate webhook\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n--------------------------------------------------\\\\\\\\nKey Changes vs v1\\\\\\\\n--------------------------------------------------\\\\\\\\n• Monorepo, Vercel CI/CD, Tailwind, Husky remain unchanged.  \\\\\\\\n• Removed TinaCMS steps and variables.  \\\\\\\\n• Added ISR revalidation endpoint and Firestore versioning as Git replacement.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n--------------------------------------------------\\\\\\\\nOpen Coordination Points (re-validated)\\\\\\\\n--------------------------------------------------\\\\\\\\n• FE: confirm TipTap UI + ISR strategy acceptable.  \\\\\\\\n• BE: supply preferred retention policy for content history.  \\\\\\\\n• Security: decide if board logins limited to organization email domain.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n--------------------------------------------------\\\\\\\\nEND OF REPORT\\\\\\\"\\\\n    }\\\\n  ]\\\\n}\\\"\\n}\\n###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-28T00:21:37.862Z###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###phase1###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: PHASE\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"justification\\\": \\\"Directors have supplied refined, inter-locking architectural plans aligned with the user’s clarified requirements (Firebase-backed admin dashboard, Resident & Board roles, no Git CMS, minimal branding). All blocking questions are resolved. We now have a clear, file-level task list that can be executed deterministically by subordinate agents (OFAAT). Moving to the Execution phase will let each Director begin shipping the initial scaffold, security rules, and infrastructure docs, providing rapid tangible value and enabling early integration testing.\\\",\\n  \\\"depString\\\": \\\"DETERMINISTIC EXECUTION PLAN (DEP) – HOA WEBSITE, PHASE 1\\\\n────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\\\\nGlobal Conventions\\\\n• Monorepo root: <repo>\\\\n• PNPM workspaces.\\\\n• All code pushed via PRs targeting main branch.\\\\n• One physical source file or infra doc per ticket (OFAAT).\\\\n\\\\nSTEP-BY-STEP\\\\n1. DevOps (Agent 2) – Scaffold repository\\\\n   1.1 Run `pnpm create next-app web --ts --eslint --tailwind --app` inside <repo>/apps/web\\\\n   1.2 Commit baseline repo structure, Tailwind config, eslint, prettier.\\\\n   1.3 Tag git commit `scaffold-web-app`.\\\\n\\\\n2. DevOps – Write infra guide\\\\n   2.1 File: infra/firebase_cms_setup.md  (as spec’d in plan)\\\\n   2.2 Include copy-paste CLI commands, env var table, service-account generation, claim assignment, ISR webhook.\\\\n\\\\n3. Frontend (Agent 4) – Build foundational layout\\\\n   3.1 File: apps/web/app/layout.tsx – HTML skeleton, Tailwind classes, imports globals.css.\\\\n   3.2 File: apps/web/styles/globals.css – Tailwind base + extended palette (hoaGreen, hoaBeige).\\\\n\\\\n4. Frontend – Navigation chrome\\\\n   4.1 File: components/Navbar.tsx – responsive nav, auth-aware links.\\\\n   4.2 File: components/Footer.tsx – simple footer with HOA name & year.\\\\n\\\\n5. Backend (Agent 3) – Security rules skeleton\\\\n   5.1 File: firestore.rules – resident vs board collections as per v2 outline.\\\\n   5.2 File: storage.rules   – bucket rules mirroring Firestore.\\\\n   5.3 Emulator test plan in comments.\\\\n\\\\n6. Backend – Firebase initialization helpers\\\\n   6.1 File: apps/web/lib/firebase.ts        – client SDK init.\\\\n   6.2 File: apps/web/lib/firebaseAdmin.ts   – Admin SDK singleton reading env vars.\\\\n\\\\n7. Frontend – Auth context\\\\n   7.1 File: contexts/AuthContext.tsx – onAuthStateChanged, role claim handling.\\\\n   7.2 File: hooks/useAuth.ts – consumer hook.\\\\n   7.3 File: middleware.ts  – edge auth + role guard for /(protected) and /(board).\\\\n\\\\n8. Backend – First API route\\\\n   8.1 File: pages/api/board/news.ts (POST) – create/update news post; verifies board role.\\\\n\\\\n9. Frontend – Auth pages\\\\n   9.1 File: app/(auth)/login/page.tsx\\\\n   9.2 File: app/(auth)/signup/page.tsx\\\\n\\\\n10. Frontend – Resident protected content shell pages (stub text)\\\\n   10.1 dues, annual-meetings, news-events.\\\\n\\\\n11. Frontend – Board dashboard Layout & home stub\\\\n   11.1 File: app/(board)/layout.tsx (BoardLayout + RoleGuard)\\\\n   11.2 File: app/(board)/page.tsx (dashboard home)\\\\n\\\\n12. Integration smoke test locally with Firebase Emulator Suite.\\\\n\\\\nAfter Step 12 we will cycle back to Planning to flesh out next increments (Post editor, Minutes uploader, etc.).\\\\n\\\\nAll agents will follow OFAAT, opening PRs in the order above, awaiting review before proceeding to their next file.\\\"\\n}\\n###phase1###\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-28T00:22:35.692Z###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Operations Department, System Call Directorate\\nTo: 1\\nType: Call Results\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"result\\\": \\\"{\\\\n  \\\\\\\"results\\\\\\\": [\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"callID\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"phase1\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"DENIED_BY_INTERNAL_REVIEW\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"details\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Phase shift was denied by internal review. Feedback from Partagaz D:\\\\\\\\nDENY  \\\\\\\\nThe plan is only a skeleton (“Phase 1”) and omits multiple core requirements the user explicitly asked for: Contact Us, Bylaws, and Schools pages; an admin/news editor UI; document upload and viewing for meeting minutes & financials; a contact form; Vercel deployment instructions; and full Firebase role/claim setup. It therefore does not yet fulfill the user’s stated needs, so cannot be approved as a complete deterministically-executable solution.\\\\\\\\nDENY\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nThis DEP is denied for the following reasons:\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n1.  **Incomplete Scope:** The DEP fails to include the creation of several pages explicitly requested by the user. The public pages `Contact Us`, `Bylaws`, and `Schools` are entirely missing from the plan. A successful project delivery must include all requested top-level pages.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n2.  **Failure to Meet Core Functional Requirement:** The user's most critical functional requirement was for an easy-to-use admin dashboard for board members to manage \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"News & Events\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" without technical knowledge. The DEP explicitly defers the creation of the \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Post editor\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" to a future phase, only building a backend API endpoint. An API endpoint alone is unusable by a non-technical board member, rendering the primary content management feature of the website non-functional. The product delivered after this phase would not satisfy the user's request.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n3.  **Technical Inconsistency:** The DEP specifies scaffolding a Next.js project with the `app` router (Step 1.1) but later specifies an API route using the outdated `pages` router convention (`pages/api/...`, Step 8.1). The correct path for an API route in the `app` router is `app/api/.../route.ts`. This inconsistency demonstrates a lack of attention to detail in the plan.\\\\\\\\nDENY\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nThe DEP lacks several critical elements needed for a deterministic execution plan:\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n1. *