nType: PHASE\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"justification\\\": \\\"Directors have supplied refined, inter-locking architectural plans aligned with the user’s clarified requirements (Firebase-backed admin dashboard, Resident & Board roles, no Git CMS, minimal branding). All blocking questions are resolved. We now have a clear, file-level task list that can be executed deterministically by subordinate agents (OFAAT). Moving to the Execution phase will let each Director begin shipping the initial scaffold, security rules, and infrastructure docs, providing rapid tangible value and enabling early integration testing.\\\",\\n  \\\"depString\\\": \\\"DETERMINISTIC EXECUTION PLAN (DEP) – HOA WEBSITE, PHASE 1\\\\n────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\\\\nGlobal Conventions\\\\n• Monorepo root: <repo>\\\\n• PNPM workspaces.\\\\n• All code pushed via PRs targeting main branch.\\\\n• One physical source file or infra doc per ticket (OFAAT).\\\\n\\\\nSTEP-BY-STEP\\\\n1. DevOps (Agent 2) – Scaffold repository\\\\n   1.1 Run `pnpm create next-app web --ts --eslint --tailwind --app` inside <repo>/apps/web\\\\n   1.2 Commit baseline repo structure, Tailwind config, eslint, prettier.\\\\n   1.3 Tag git commit `scaffold-web-app`.\\\\n\\\\n2. DevOps – Write infra guide\\\\n   2.1 File: infra/firebase_cms_setup.md  (as spec’d in plan)\\\\n   2.2 Include copy-paste CLI commands, env var table, service-account generation, claim assignment, ISR webhook.\\\\n\\\\n3. Frontend (Agent 4) – Build foundational layout\\\\n   3.1 File: apps/web/app/layout.tsx – HTML skeleton, Tailwind classes, imports globals.css.\\\\n   3.2 File: apps/web/styles/globals.css – Tailwind base + extended palette (hoaGreen, hoaBeige).\\\\n\\\\n4. Frontend – Navigation chrome\\\\n   4.1 File: components/Navbar.tsx – responsive nav, auth-aware links.\\\\n   4.2 File: components/Footer.tsx – simple footer with HOA name & year.\\\\n\\\\n5. Backend (Agent 3) – Security rules skeleton\\\\n   5.1 File: firestore.rules – resident vs board collections as per v2 outline.\\\\n   5.2 File: storage.rules   – bucket rules mirroring Firestore.\\\\n   5.3 Emulator test plan in comments.\\\\n\\\\n6. Backend – Firebase initialization helpers\\\\n   6.1 File: apps/web/lib/firebase.ts        – client SDK init.\\\\n   6.2 File: apps/web/lib/firebaseAdmin.ts   – Admin SDK singleton reading env vars.\\\\n\\\\n7. Frontend – Auth context\\\\n   7.1 File: contexts/AuthContext.tsx – onAuthStateChanged, role claim handling.\\\\n   7.2 File: hooks/useAuth.ts – consumer hook.\\\\n   7.3 File: middleware.ts  – edge auth + role guard for /(protected) and /(board).\\\\n\\\\n8. Backend – First API route\\\\n   8.1 File: pages/api/board/news.ts (POST) – create/update news post; verifies board role.\\\\n\\\\n9. Frontend – Auth pages\\\\n   9.1 File: app/(auth)/login/page.tsx\\\\n   9.2 File: app/(auth)/signup/page.tsx\\\\n\\\\n10. Frontend – Resident protected content shell pages (stub text)\\\\n   10.1 dues, annual-meetings, news-events.\\\\n\\\\n11. Frontend – Board dashboard Layout & home stub\\\\n   11.1 File: app/(board)/layout.tsx (BoardLayout + RoleGuard)\\\\n   11.2 File: app/(board)/page.tsx (dashboard home)\\\\n\\\\n12. Integration smoke test locally with Firebase Emulator Suite.\\\\n\\\\nAfter Step 12 we will cycle back to Planning to flesh out next increments (Post editor, Minutes uploader, etc.).\\\\n\\\\nAll agents will follow OFAAT, opening PRs in the order above, awaiting review before proceeding to their next file.\\\"\\n}\\n###phase1###\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-28T00:22:35.692Z###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Operations Department, System Call Directorate\\nTo: 1\\nType: Call Results\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"result\\\": \\\"{\\\\n  \\\\\\\"results\\\\\\\": [\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"callID\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"phase1\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"DENIED_BY_INTERNAL_REVIEW\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"details\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Phase shift was denied by internal review. Feedback from Partagaz D:\\\\\\\\nDENY  \\\\\\\\nThe plan is only a skeleton (“Phase 1”) and omits multiple core requirements the user explicitly asked for: Contact Us, Bylaws, and Schools pages; an admin/news editor UI; document upload and viewing for meeting minutes & financials; a contact form; Vercel deployment instructions; and full Firebase role/claim setup. It therefore does not yet fulfill the user’s stated needs, so cannot be approved as a complete deterministically-executable solution.\\\\\\\\nDENY\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nThis DEP is denied for the following reasons:\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n1.  **Incomplete Scope:** The DEP fails to include the creation of several pages explicitly requested by the user. The public pages `Contact Us`, `Bylaws`, and `Schools` are entirely missing from the plan. A successful project delivery must include all requested top-level pages.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n2.  **Failure to Meet Core Functional Requirement:** The user's most critical functional requirement was for an easy-to-use admin dashboard for board members to manage \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"News & Events\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" without technical knowledge. The DEP explicitly defers the creation of the \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Post editor\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" to a future phase, only building a backend API endpoint. An API endpoint alone is unusable by a non-technical board member, rendering the primary content management feature of the website non-functional. The product delivered after this phase would not satisfy the user's request.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n3.  **Technical Inconsistency:** The DEP specifies scaffolding a Next.js project with the `app` router (Step 1.1) but later specifies an API route using the outdated `pages` router convention (`pages/api/...`, Step 8.1). The correct path for an API route in the `app` router is `app/api/.../route.ts`. This inconsistency demonstrates a lack of attention to detail in the plan.\\\\\\\\nDENY\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nThe DEP lacks several critical elements needed for a deterministic execution plan:\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n1. **Missing Core Pages**: The user explicitly requested Contact Us, Bylaws, and Schools pages, but these are not included in the DEP. Only the protected pages (Dues, Annual Meetings, News & Events) are mentioned as \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"stub pages.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n2. **Incomplete Admin Dashboard**: The user specifically requested \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"a simple admin dashboard or editor\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" for board members to update content without coding knowledge. While the DEP mentions a \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Board dashboard Layout & home stub,\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" it doesn't include the actual content management functionality that was the core requirement.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n3. **Missing Contact Form**: The user requested \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"a contact form for residents to reach out with questions or concerns\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" but this is not implemented in the DEP.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n4. **Insufficient API Routes**: Only one API route (/api/board/news.ts) is defined, but the user needs full CRUD operations for managing News & Events, updating other protected content, and handling contact form submissions.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n5. **No Data Models**: The DEP doesn't define Firestore collections/documents structure for storing news posts, meeting minutes, financial reports, or other content types.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n6. **Missing File Upload Functionality**: The user needs to upload \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"meeting minutes, financial reports\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" but there's no implementation for file handling or storage.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n7. **Incomplete Authentication Flow**: While auth pages are created, there's no API route for user registration approval or role assignment, which would be needed for an HOA system.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nThe DEP appears to be only a partial implementation that would not satisfy the user's requirements for a functional HOA website with content management capabilities.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    }\\\\n  ]\\\\n}\\\"\\n}\\n###CAL